+# Receipts stopped
+
+For the volunteer on call when members say their receipts stopped arriving. Starts the receipts worker again and
+sends the receipts that queued up while it was down; until then, members who paid get no receipt. Written after
+receipts stopped for the third time, on the night of October 29, 2026, and the volunteer on call had nothing to
+follow. The first time, members waited until noon for Tomás to wake up. The second time, on September 14, Tomás found
+that the [worker](../architecture.md#parts) had been stopped since a deploy the night before: the deploy script
+restarts only the web app. Owner: Tomás.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- A shell on the larder server, with `sudo` for `systemctl` and access to the `larder` database through `psql`.
+- A copy of this repository on the server, for `scripts/restart-receipts-worker`.
+
+## Steps
+
+1. Run `scripts/restart-receipts-worker`. It shows the worker's state and the jobs waiting, starts the worker, then
+   checks every minute until no receipt is waiting. It takes a few minutes: the worker sends about 40 receipts a
+   minute.
+
+   Expected: first `Worker: inactive` or `Worker: failed`, then a `todo:` count that goes down each minute, and at
+   the end `Done: the worker is running and no receipts are waiting.` A few `failed` jobs may be left; on
+   September 14 the 3 failed were receipts to members without a valid email address, which no restart will send.
+2. Ask a member who reported it whether their receipt arrived.
+
+   Expected: they have it.
+
+## If it fails
+
+- `The worker is already running`: the worker is up but receipts still don't arrive, which is not the stop this
+  runbook covers. Keep the log the script printed and ask Tomás.
+- `The worker stopped again` or `todo has not gone down`: the script prints the last 50 lines of the worker's log,
+  `journalctl -u larder-worker -n 50`. Keep them and ask Tomás.
+- Whatever happened, add what you found to this page, so the next volunteer has it.
